  "name": "capture-mask-coverage-modes",
  "description": "capture.result.frame.maskCoverage {mode, reasons} says which mask mode applied to a native frame: precise, wholeHost (a toolkit host masked whole, the Compose default), or wholeFrame, with reasons from a closed set. When the engine accepts such a frame it records a capture_diagnostic {component: capture_masking, frameId, mode, reasons} right after the frame, always (here without the captureDiagnostics capability), so Atlas can tell a whole-masked frame from a broken capture. The frame record never carries the coverage. A frame without maskCoverage records nothing new.",
